You are proposing a change to a researcher-governed ontology. Do not change it.
Compare the selected Knowledge Cards with the current Facet–Type ontology. Some
cards are new and untyped; others already have Types and are being revalidated.

The ontology graph contains Type nodes and Type-to-Type relations. A Facet is only
a stereotype/color grouping of Types. A card may receive multiple Types.
Prefer existing Types. Create a Type only when its definition cannot be expressed
by an existing Type. For every selected card, return the complete desired Type set,
not merely additions. Omitting a currently assigned Type means removing it in the
new version. A card may have multiple Types. Put every reviewed card ID in
reviewed_card_ids, including a card whose desired Type set is empty.
Follow the researcher comment when it requests a Type name/description update or a
Type relation add/update/delete. Preserve stable IDs for updates and deletions.

